---
title: 'Fills & Borders'
---

This section describes how to change the fills and borders of chart elements.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Fills & Borders" name="fills-borders" type="generated" /%}

In the above example:

-   A black border is drawn around the series area with a corner radius and no padding.
-   A border, fill and corner radius are applied to the [Legend](./legend), with padding between the border and items provided as a single number.
-   A border, fill and corner radius are applied to the series labels and [axis labels](./axes-labels) with padding defined for each of the top, right, bottom and left.

## Fills

```js
label: {
    color: '#333333', //font colour
    fill: '#e0e0e0', // fill colour
    fillOpacity: 0.8,
}
```

See [Series Fills](./fills) for details of the available fills types, including [patterns](./fills/#patterns) and [gradients](/fills/#gradients).

## Borders

```js
border: {
    enabled: true,
    stroke: '#FCA441',
    strokeWidth: 2,
},
```

## Padding

Padding can be defined as a single number to be applied to all sides of the element, or as an object with values for `top`, `right`, `bottom` and `left`.

```js
padding: 4; //padding of 4px on all sides
```

```js
padding: {
    top: 4,
    right: 6,
    bottom: 2,
    left: 6
},
```

